    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Like many Boone County towns, Bergman grew around the White River Division Railway, later part of the Missouri Pacific Line.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bergman%2C_Arkansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Bergman first incorporated on August 4, 1905, and re-incorporated on March 14, 1968.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bergman%2C_Arkansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The town’s first postmistress was Bergman herself, and a new post office opened in 1974.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
